Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Depack internal i386 backend records for the tp2cc-translated bootstrap
License: expat

These records carry no file-format role -- they are internal i386
backend state and tables, not written to PPU files or to disk in any
other form.  Upstream declared them `packed' only to save RAM on
1990s-era builds.

tp2cc translates Pascal `packed record' to `struct [[gnu::packed]]' in
the translated bootstrap.  Unlike `#pragma pack(push,1)', the attribute form makes gcc
reject binding a C++ reference to a misaligned member, which is
exactly what a Pascal `var' parameter pointing at
`treference.offset' or `tlocation.register' becomes under the
translated lowering: gcc diagnoses `cannot bind packed field X to T&' at
compile time. For aggregate carriers such as `tinsentry.optypes' and
`TInsProp.Ch', C++ will happily compile the packed field access and
then execute through a misaligned subobject/reference at runtime.

On native x86 the original code worked because the CPU tolerates
unaligned loads; in the translated bootstrap the resulting references are undefined
regardless of hardware.  Depacking these in-memory records restores
natural alignment without disturbing any on-disk layout, and leaves
`[[gnu::packed]]' enforced for records that really are file formats
(`ppuheader', `tsymbol', `tarhdr', ...).

--- a/compiler/i386/cpubase.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/cpubase.pas
@@ -455,7 +455,11 @@
 
   { immediate/reference record }
   preference = ^treference;
-  treference = packed record
+  { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc-translated bootstrap. This record
+    is in-memory-only (no file-format role), and packing it forced misaligned
+    access to its `longint`/pointer fields. C++ references to those fields
+    are UB when misaligned, which `[[gnu::packed]]` rightly rejects. }
+  treference = record
      is_immediate : boolean; { is this used as reference or immediate }
      segment,
      base,
@@ -507,7 +511,8 @@
   );
 
   plocation = ^tlocation;
-  tlocation = packed record
+  { depacked for tp2cc bootstrap, see note on `treference` above. }
+  tlocation = record
      case loc : tloc of
         LOC_MEM,LOC_REFERENCE : (reference : treference);
         LOC_FPU : ();
@@ -579,7 +584,13 @@
 
 {$ifndef NOAG386BIN}
 type
-  tinsentry=packed record
+  { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc-translated bootstrap. This
+    instruction-table entry is in-memory-only, and packing it misaligns
+    the `longint` operand-type array. tp2cc lowers that array to a translated
+    aggregate carrier whose indexed element access binds references to
+    the underlying elements; keeping this record packed therefore turns
+    normal operand-table lookups into misaligned-reference UB. }
+  tinsentry=record
     opcode  : tasmop;
     ops     : byte;
     optypes : array[0..2] of longint;
@@ -648,7 +659,11 @@
 const
   MaxCh = 3; { Max things a instruction can change }
 type
-  TInsProp = packed record
+  { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc-translated bootstrap. This is
+    optimizer metadata, not an on-disk format, and its change-array is
+    only consulted in memory. Keeping it packed forces aggregate indexed
+    access through a packed subobject for no file-format benefit. }
+  TInsProp = record
     Ch : Array[1..MaxCh] of TInsChange;
   end;
